# Scraped content -- other people's forum posts and product renders.
# All of it regenerates from a single `python scrape.py` run.
images/
cache-board*.json
covers-board*.json
feed-board*.html
feed-vendors.html

# Signing keys, anywhere in the tree. A private release key must never land in
# a public repo: it is the identity every release is signed with.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.jks.b64
android/debug.keystore

# The one deliberate exception. android/public-release.keystore is committed on
# purpose and its password is "android", written down in the README -- it is a
# published key, not a leaked one. Android only lets an APK install over one
# signed with the same key, so the key has to be *stable*; this repo trades
# secrecy for having nothing to configure. Anyone can therefore build an APK
# this app accepts as an update, which is the accepted cost. Swap in a private
# key by setting the KEYSTORE_BASE64 and KEYSTORE_PASSWORD secrets, which take
# precedence -- see "Release signing" in the README.
!android/public-release.keystore

# Build output. The APK is published by the release workflow rather than
# committed, so the repo never disagrees with the Releases page.
android/build/
android/*.apk
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.tmp

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
android/*.idsig
